Ladybird gives ::file-selector-button the system font at the size
of the input’s font, and resets the letter-spacing, word-spacing,
text-transform, text-indent, text-shadow, white-space, and text-align
it would inherit. In Blink and WebKit, the button is an input element in
the file input’s shadow tree, which the UA rule for form controls gives
their control font, and their UA rules for the button set “font-size:
inherit”. Gecko’s forms.css gives ::file-selector-button “font:
-moz-button”. Run in Chrome 157.0.8103.79, Firefox 151.0, and WebKit
26.5: all three give the button a system font at the input’s size, with
normal weight, style, and line height, and none of the input’s text
styling, except that Firefox keeps the input’s letter-spacing.
